# Never ship host installs into images: pnpm node_modules are symlinks into
# version-named store paths, so a host copy would overwrite the image's own
# install with links that dangle inside the container.
**/node_modules
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/dist
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report

# Env and direnv files, npm configuration (which can hold a registry token), Claude Code
# settings and repository metadata are never part of an image's build context. The
# patterns match at any depth, because the Dockerfiles copy apps/ and packages/ whole.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc
**/.npmrc
**/.claude
**/.DS_Store
**/.git

# Planning documents and tests are not needed at runtime.
docs
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/e2e
